Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:07:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] wip/kv-residency: A3 diagnostic --
 LLAMA_KV_REGION_SPILL_SKIP (bisect one tensor's spill)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DIAGNOSTIC ONLY, unset = the shipped behaviour.  `LLAMA_KV_REGION_SPILL_SKIP=<tensor indices>` keeps the
listed tensors of a windowed buffer fully resident, so the open finding (a spilled KV changes the numbers on
a 27B, wip/kv-residency/A2-MIXED-BACKING.md §3.7.6) can be bisected over tensors instead of guessed at.

First ladder on the 27B Q4_K_XL -c 8192 q8_0 arm (64 tokens, plain = 305 chars e2cea6fa6670):
  every tensor skipped (no spill at all)      305 chars e2cea6fa6670   <- the control: inert when nothing spills
  ONLY tensor 0 spills (4 MiB, one tensor)    310 chars ccdb98b7b254   <- one tensor is enough
  tensors 0..15 spill                         317 chars df3128cb54d5
  all 32 tensors spill                        325 chars fb65430049e9

So the difference is not scale-dependent and not a stress effect: a single 4 MiB tensor spill moves the text,
while the flip's byte round-trip verifies.  That points the next session at the flip's stage-OUT (the existing
verify compares stage vs restore, which is blind to a stage filled with the wrong data) or at a lost kernel
store into host-backed memory -- see §3.7.6.

Also: the VMM selftest's PASS line now describes what it checks (partial flips are REFUSED).

Not delivery work.
